CM_ "Fisker Ocean mid-range radar (MRR) private CAN-FD bus (panda bus 1). Draft, reverse-engineered from route 6bdf6a23860be7bd/000000b5--bfe13ac451 (61 s, low-speed parking-lot drive). Not in the FM29 ADASBUS matrix. E2E on most frames: CRC-8 poly 0x1D, init 0, xorout 0, computed over [DataID] + bytes 1..N, same scheme as fiskercan.fisker_plain_checksum. Object slots are documented on MRR_Obj00 and are identical for MRR_Obj01..31.";
CM_ BO_ 256 "AUTOSAR CanTSyn global time, 10 Hz SYNC/FUP pairs. Type 0x20 = SYNC (TimeValue = seconds), 0x28 = FUP (TimeValue = nanoseconds). The MRR timestamps in 0x300/0x500 are in this time base.";
CM_ BO_ 512 "Ego motion fed to the MRR, 100 Hz. E2E CRC8 (0x1D) DataID 64 over bytes 1..28; SecOC MAC in bytes 29..31. Bytes 5-10 are zero on this car; bytes 15-17 (0x402290) and 21-22 carry constants.";
CM_ SG_ 512 ADAS_MRR_VehSpd "Unsigned speed, = carState.vEgo*3.6 exactly (wheel-speed based, ~3% below GPS on this car). Direction in ADAS_MRR_DrvDir.";
CM_ SG_ 512 ADAS_MRR_YawRate "Same encoding as YRS_YawRate on ADASBUS; positive = left (CCW).";
CM_ BO_ 513 "Wheel speeds/directions/pulse counters to the MRR, 50 Hz. E2E DataID 65 over bytes 1..19. Bytes 17-19 constant 0x4FC984. Pulse-counter wheel order assumed FL,FR,RL,RR.";
CM_ BO_ 514 "Vehicle clock, 1 Hz. E2E DataID 67. Hour/minute/second verified against GPS (UTC; car clock ~8 s ahead). The upper 17 bits (0x1609 throughout the log) are probably the date but did not decode as a calendar. Bytes 7, 9, 10 vary and are unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 768 "Radar cycle header, one per 65.01 ms cycle, sent before the 32 object slots. E2E DataID 16.";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_ObjListTime_Sec "Global (CanTSyn) time of the object list; ~54 ms before the frame is received.";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_MeasTime_Sec "Global (CanTSyn) time of the measurement/scan; ~131 ms before the frame is received, ~78 ms before ObjListTime. Same value as MRR_Env_MeasTime in 0x500.";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_Hdr_Unk_B11 "Constant 0x4750.";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_CycleCounter "Same value as MRR_ObjNN_CycleCounter in the slots of this cycle.";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_NumObjects "Number of populated slots in 0x310-0x32F this cycle (matched 937/937 cycles).";
CM_ SG_ 768 MRR_LocalTime_Sec "Radar free-running clock: seconds + SubSec (256 ns ticks). Exactly 65.0117 ms per cycle, ~1.34 s behind MeasTime and drifting ~30 ppm.";
CM_ BO_ 769 "50 Hz, E2E DataID 53 (radar DataID range). Payload constant 0x01 0x00 in this log.";
CM_ BO_ 784 "Object slot 0. E2E DataID 17.";
CM_ BO_ 785 "Object slot 1. E2E DataID 18.";
CM_ BO_ 786 "Object slot 2. E2E DataID 19.";
CM_ BO_ 787 "Object slot 3. E2E DataID 20.";
CM_ BO_ 788 "Object slot 4. E2E DataID 21.";
CM_ BO_ 789 "Object slot 5. E2E DataID 22.";
CM_ BO_ 790 "Object slot 6. E2E DataID 23.";
CM_ BO_ 791 "Object slot 7. E2E DataID 24.";
CM_ BO_ 792 "Object slot 8. E2E DataID 25.";
CM_ BO_ 793 "Object slot 9. E2E DataID 26.";
CM_ BO_ 794 "Object slot 10. E2E DataID 27.";
CM_ BO_ 795 "Object slot 11. E2E DataID 28.";
CM_ BO_ 796 "Object slot 12. E2E DataID 29.";
CM_ BO_ 797 "Object slot 13. E2E DataID 30.";
CM_ BO_ 798 "Object slot 14. E2E DataID 32.";
CM_ BO_ 799 "Object slot 15. E2E DataID 33.";
CM_ BO_ 800 "Object slot 16. E2E DataID 34.";
CM_ BO_ 801 "Object slot 17. E2E DataID 35.";
CM_ BO_ 802 "Object slot 18. E2E DataID 36.";
CM_ BO_ 803 "Object slot 19. E2E DataID 37.";
CM_ BO_ 804 "Object slot 20. E2E DataID 38.";
CM_ BO_ 805 "Object slot 21. E2E DataID 39.";
CM_ BO_ 806 "Object slot 22. E2E DataID 40.";
CM_ BO_ 807 "Object slot 23. E2E DataID 41.";
CM_ BO_ 808 "Object slot 24. E2E DataID 42.";
CM_ BO_ 809 "Object slot 25. E2E DataID 43.";
CM_ BO_ 810 "Object slot 26. E2E DataID 44.";
CM_ BO_ 811 "Object slot 27. E2E DataID 45.";
CM_ BO_ 812 "Object slot 28. E2E DataID 46.";
CM_ BO_ 813 "Object slot 29. E2E DataID 48.";
CM_ BO_ 814 "Object slot 30. E2E DataID 49.";
CM_ BO_ 815 "Object slot 31. E2E DataID 50 over bytes 1..44; SecOC MAC in bytes 45..47 (freshness byte 44 = 0 throughout the log).";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_ID "Persistent track ID (increments for new tracks, wraps in 11 bits so far). Empty slot = ID 0, byte 5 = 0x40, bytes 6..43 = 0. Slots fill from 0x310 upward, roughly oldest track first.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Unk_B5 "Always 1, including empty slots.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_MeasHistory "Shift register, LSB = this cycle: 1 = track got a detection, 0 = coasted.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_State "Rises 0->3 as a track matures; drops right before a track is deleted.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Quality "13 for mature stationary tracks, 5-10 otherwise; meaning unknown.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Age "Radar cycles (65 ms) since track creation; MeasHistory has (Age-3) valid bits.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_DistLong "x, forward from the radar. Scale checked against GPS (0.0503 m/bit).";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_DistLat "y, POSITIVE = RIGHT (openpilot yRel = -DistLat). Sign from ego-odometry fits in turns; scale 0.05 matches but only to ~10%.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_VrelLong "Relative velocity. Stationary targets read -ADAS_MRR_VehSpd at 0.06 (16.7 raw per m/s), but that speed is wheel speed, 3.1% under GPS: against GPS they fit 0.0618-0.0631, i.e. 0.0625 (1/16). The web HUD world model applies 0.0625/0.06 (world_model.MEASURED_CALIBRATION). The scale stays 0.06 here on purpose: it matches carState.vEgo (wheel speed), so radard's vLead = vRel + vEgo is ~0 for stationary targets.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_VrelLat "Positive = right. Translational only: stationary targets stay ~0 in turns.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_ArelLong "Scale ~0.031 m/s2 per bit from -aEgo on stationary targets; 0.03 vs 1/32 not resolved.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_DistLong_Std "6-bit uncertainty code (monotonic, smaller = better), scale unknown. Same for all *_Std.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_DistCorr "Probably a correlation term, ~30 for stationary in-path targets. Same for VrelCorr/ArelCorr.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_DynProp "Observed: 5 = stationary (ego moving), 2 = stationary/slow while ego stopped or reversing, 7 = mostly crossing/moving, 1/3/4/6 = moving, 8 = far/uncertain.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Heading "Over-ground heading, clockwise positive, raw 128 = parallel to ego (fit corr 0.997 vs velocity direction). 127 = default for unclassified tracks, 255 = n/a.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Unk_B28 "127 for unclassified tracks, 0/255 or 40-125 for classified ones; maybe heading quality.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Width "Tentative 0.2 m: crossing car 10-13 (2.0-2.6 m), pedestrian 4 (0.8 m). 0 for unclassified tracks.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Length "Tentative 0.2 m: crossing car grows 8->24 (1.6->4.8 m) as more is seen, pedestrian 2 (0.4 m).";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Class "Observed: 0 = unclassified point target, 1 = car-sized, 6 = pedestrian-sized, 8 = small object (0.4-1.2 m), 3/5 rare.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Status "Bitfield-like: 1 and 4 on unclassified tracks, 12 on classified ones, others rare.";
CM_ SG_ 784 MRR_Obj00_Unk_B35 "Constant 0x0A70 (bytes 35-36 read 0x29C3 / 0xA9C3 including neighbors).";
CM_ BO_ 1024 "Radar ego-motion state, one per radar cycle. No E2E (bytes 0-2 = 0). Fields are offset-binary around mid-scale. Scales are fits against 0x200.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_EgoSpeed "Signed (negative in reverse). Fit 0.003044; 100/32767 assumed.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_EgoYawRate "Positive = clockwise (right), radar frame. Fit 0.1837 deg/s/bit.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_EgoYawRateFine "Positive = clockwise. Fit 0.02204 deg/s/bit (corr 0.996).";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_EgoCurvature "Positive = right. Saturates at +/-8191 raw (radius < ~10 m) in tight low-speed turns.";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_EgoCurvState "2 = straight, 1 = turning, 0 = tight turn (curvature saturated).";
CM_ SG_ 1024 MRR_Ego_Unk_B9 "Constant 0x7FFF (mid-scale / unused).";
CM_ BO_ 1025 "20 bytes, one per radar cycle, all zero in this log.";
CM_ BO_ 1026 "One per radar cycle, no E2E. Otherwise constant: 00 00 00 03 00 xx ... 00 01 00 01 ... yy ... 01 at byte 43.";
CM_ SG_ 1026 MRR_402_B5 "Varies 5-43 and rises with speed (r=0.61). Maybe a raw detection count.";
CM_ SG_ 1026 MRR_402_B19 "Rises slowly 27 -> 35 over the minute. Looks like a temperature.";
CM_ BO_ 1280 "One per radar cycle, E2E DataID 52. Timestamp = MRR_MeasTime of the same cycle (1/4096 s). Bytes 7-12 / 13-18 / 19-28 / 29-34 / 35-39 are blocks that sit at fixed fill patterns (7FBFF83F79FB, FFFFFBFFFFF8, 00000003FDFFC1FBCFDF, FFFFDFFFFFC0, 0000000000) when invalid and get filled in ~30-43% of cycles. Not decoded. Their contents do not copy any object-slot field.";
CM_ BO_ 1536 "1 Hz, E2E DataID 51 (radar DataID range). Payload constant 00 78 FD 80 44 04 58 01 64 80 41 50 AF FF E8 00 00 00. Probably mounting/calibration/version data.";
BA_DEF_ BO_  "VFrameFormat" ENUM  "StandardCAN","ExtendedCAN","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","reserved","StandardCAN_FD","ExtendedCAN_FD";
